hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
|> [c8730752@cc.nu.oz.au writes:]
|> [] I hate *hate* this! Why must Nethack 3.09 check the date of the
save file?
|> 
|> hmmm, good point.  it checks the date as an indirect means of
determining
|> version (so old, incompatible versions don't get used).  perhaps it
should
|> simply encode version and check for that (so that silly machines that
can't
|> keep track of time properly don't suffer).

That's probably a reasonable fix.  But I have never understood why the
Dev Team has designed the game so that minor errors turn into major
disasters.  How much extra work would it be to *prompt the user*
before deleting the old save file?  Deleting a file because you don't
understand its format or don't approve of its date strikes me as an
arrogant decision.  Imagine if your favorite text editor decided to
delete your files whenever they were found to be out of date (or have
the wrong version stamp).

